  "CARB-NCERT-4-LONG-001": { status: "hold", note: "third audit (review checklist): The question says 'Draw the electron dot structures' for four species. The answer is only a verbal description. It has no actual dot structures and does not show the lone pairs on O in ethanoic acid or propanone." },
  "CARB-NCERT-4-SA-004": { status: "publish", hash: "8d2fa4e30f20ccc1", note: "book check MATCH, text faithful; syllabus IN (guard); blind solve agrees; judge + text/steps audit clean; second audit clean; third audit (review checklist) clean or kept by its written rule" },
  "CARB-NCERT-4-LONG-002": { status: "hold", note: "third audit (review checklist): The explanation of the boiling point as an 'H-bonded dimer' is not in the NCERT chapter. The sodium-metal comparison ('acid reacts vigorously, alcohol slowly', and the reaction of sodium with the acid) is also not taught in the chapter. The 16.6°C figure differs from the chapter's 290 K." },
  "CARB-NCERT-4-VSA-012": { status: "publish", hash: "da7f0c108aac53cc", note: "book check MATCH, text faithful; syllabus IN (guard); blind solve agrees; judge + text/steps audit clean; second audit clean; third audit (review checklist) clean or kept by its written rule" },
  "CARB-NCERT-4-VSA-013": { status: "hold", note: "third audit (review checklist): The answer relies on 'calorific value' and 'easy to transport' and 'sustained heat'. None of these appear in the NCERT chapter." },
  "CARB-NCERT-4-SA-005": { status: "publish", hash: "f8d6a07abfdef04d", note: "book check MATCH, text faithful; syllabus IN (guard); blind solve agrees; judge + text/steps audit clean; second audit clean; third audit (review checklist) clean or kept by its written rule" },
  "CARB-NCERT-4-VSA-014": { status: "hold", note: "judge/audit: The litmus result is right, but the key text has a drafting error: 'acidic ROOH + strong base NaOH' uses the wrong formula (should be RCOOH, a weak acid). Clean up the wording." },
  "CARB-NCERT-4-VSA-015": { status: "hold", note: "third audit (review checklist): The answer names Pt as a catalyst; the chapter names only palladium or nickel. It also introduces 'vanaspati ghee', which the chapter does not mention." },
